	(text "BEACON Phone Module - inferred specifications (no spec doc supplied; derived from the Altium schematic)\n  * Plugs straight into the phone through a USB-C plug: USB 2.0 FS data + 5 V power (<= 500 mA).\n  * Illuminates the backscatter wearable with a 2.4 GHz ISM CW carrier: LMX2582 -> CC2595 PA, about +20 dBm\n    conducted into a U.FL for a Taoglas FXP70.07.0053A flex antenna, low-pass filtered for harmonics.\n  * Receives the backscattered signal on a Taoglas WDP.2458 ceramic patch: BPF -> QPL9547 LNA -> nRF52840.\n  * Housed in a MagSafe puck (beacon_phone_magsafe_2p5mm.scad): 55 x 78.45 mm board, 4x M2, USB-C cable to the phone.\n  * nRF52840 controls the synth (SPI), PA_EN, LNA shutdown and the USB link; it reads two INA219 monitors\n    (5 V input and 3.3 V rail).\n  * 3.3 V rail from an LT80602 Silent Switcher buck; expected load about 0.45 A.\nTop-sheet TODOs from the Altium file: RX/TX antenna connectors added; PA GND connected; MCU and CW synth completed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
